        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-30 04:05:49.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20565 tests: use EC_* layouts in sanity-ec layout tests",
        "message": "LU-20565 tests: use EC_* layouts in sanity-ec layout tests\n\nsanity-ec subtests 1f, 1h, 1k, 2b, 2f, 7b, 7c and 21c hard-coded an\nEC 4+2 or 3+1 layout, most with a gate of 6 to 8 OSTs, although they\nonly check how parity components follow the data components, how a\nparity mirror is split, or a migrate between EC layouts.  Most would\nbe skipped on the 4 and 7 OST test sessions.\n\nUse the EC_ARG, EC_DSTRIPE and EC_CSTRIPE defaults that enable_ec()\nscales to OSTCOUNT.  2b, 2f, 7b and 7c now run with 3 OSTs.  1f, 1h,\n1k and 21c mix a fixed 2+1 layout with the default one, and need 4\nOSTs so the two layouts differ.  Put each PFL boundary in front of\nan EC component on a multiple of the row width.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-ec\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-ec ostcount=4\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ibb58f4778fdd722a8cc663b8f5a6f285dd3ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
